    <p>By contrast, the <strong>1950s</strong> were the most concentrated decade for repeat winners, with five of its ten ceremonies going to composers who had already won: Dimitri Tiomkin dominated with three wins, and Franz Waxman won back-to-back in 1950&ndash;1951. The emerging <strong>2020s</strong> are on pace to rival that concentration, with Ludwig G&ouml;ransson claiming three of the decade's first seven awards.</p>

